{"id":"5d00fb89d36e20b8","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-df-diamond-sequence.md","title":"$\\diamondsuit$ Sequence","display":"df-diamond-sequence — $\\diamondsuit$ Sequence","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-diamond-sequence","aliases":["58-df-diamond-sequence"],"display":"df-diamond-sequence — $\\diamondsuit$ Sequence","depends_on":["[[58-df-diamond]]","[[58-df-guessing]]","[[58-df-regular-cardinal]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-diamond-sequence"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-diamond-sequence</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-diamond-sequence — <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\diamondsuit\">\\(\\diamondsuit\\)</span> Sequence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d60e0a36bd259287\" href=\"?note=d60e0a36bd259287\" title=\"58-df-diamond\">58-df-diamond</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"40de677e4faaffa1\" href=\"?note=40de677e4faaffa1\" title=\"58-df-guessing\">58-df-guessing</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\\in V\">\\(\\kappa\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A_\\bullet\\in V\">\\(A_\\bullet\\in V\\)</span> (sequence of initial-segment guesses)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\)</span> (regular-cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{DiamondSequence}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\operatorname{DiamondSequence}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (stationary-set diamond sequence, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"40de677e4faaffa1\" href=\"?note=40de677e4faaffa1\" title=\"58-df-guessing\">58-df-guessing</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FullDiamondSequence}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{FullDiamondSequence}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (full-domain witness predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}diamond\\text{-}sequence} \\vdash \\mathrm{FullDiamondSequence}_S(A_\\bullet,\\kappa) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega\\in\\kappa\\land\\operatorname{DiamondSequence}_S(A_\\bullet,\\kappa,\\kappa)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}diamond\\text{-}sequence} \\vdash \\mathrm{FullDiamondSequence}_S(A_\\bullet,\\kappa) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega\\in\\kappa\\land\\operatorname{DiamondSequence}_S(A_\\bullet,\\kappa,\\kappa)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}diamond\\text{-}sequence\\text{-}notation} \\vdash \\diamondsuit_\\kappa(A_\\bullet)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{FullDiamondSequence}_S(A_\\bullet,\\kappa)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}diamond\\text{-}sequence\\text{-}notation} \\vdash \\diamondsuit_\\kappa(A_\\bullet)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{FullDiamondSequence}_S(A_\\bullet,\\kappa)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}diamond\\text{-}witness} \\vdash \\diamondsuit_\\kappa\\leftrightarrow\\exists A_\\bullet\\in V\\;\\mathrm{FullDiamondSequence}_S(A_\\bullet,\\kappa)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}diamond\\text{-}witness} \\vdash \\diamondsuit_\\kappa\\leftrightarrow\\exists A_\\bullet\\in V\\;\\mathrm{FullDiamondSequence}_S(A_\\bullet,\\kappa)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The proposition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\diamondsuit_\\kappa\">\\(\\diamondsuit_\\kappa\\)</span> and a particular witness <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\diamondsuit_\\kappa(A_\\bullet)\">\\(\\diamondsuit_\\kappa(A_\\bullet)\\)</span> have different arities.  The wrapper has a distinct name and specializes the canonical three-place predicate to the full stationary domain <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S=\\kappa\">\\(S=\\kappa\\)</span>, avoiding a conflicting two-place <code>DiamondSequence_S</code>.</li>\n<li>A <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\diamondsuit\">\\(\\diamondsuit\\)</span> sequence guesses every subset of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> stationarily often.</li>\n<li>At <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa=\\omega_1\">\\(\\kappa=\\omega_1\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\diamondsuit_{\\omega_1}\">\\(\\diamondsuit_{\\omega_1}\\)</span> implies the existence of an <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1\">\\(\\omega_1\\)</span>-Suslin tree; the converse is not valid in general.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-diamond","status":"resolved","id":"d60e0a36bd259287","anc